hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"972","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one night at midnight and prayed in the mosque, so some other people also prayed behind him (this hadith has already been mentioned in the Book of Prayer; there are some different words in both these hadiths. Therefore, please refer to these hadiths: Chapter: When there is a wall or a sutrah between the imam and the people... and Chapter: The Prayer of Tahajjud...). At the end of this hadith, she says that this condition remained until the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
